# ===========================================================================
# DO NOT REMOVE THE /scripts/* UN-IGNORE LINES FURTHER DOWN.
#
# /scripts/* is ignored so developer scratch scripts stay out of the repo. The
# negations below exist because these scripts ARE CI gates: if they are not
# tracked, CI cannot run them and the suite rots again without anyone noticing.
#
#   scripts/verify_test_integrity.sh        fails CI if a test cannot report
#                                           failure
#   scripts/count_tests.sh                  the registered/verifying/incapable
#                                           census the gate is measured against
#   scripts/verify_benchmark_methodology.sh fails CI if the benchmark stops
#                                           measuring what it claims to
#   scripts/check_gate_scripts_tracked.sh   fails if any of the three above is
#                                           untracked by git, itself included
#
# This file was rewritten once already, in task 5 of the ground-truth plan. All
# four negations survived it and CI runs all four. They are kept that way by a
# run-time check rather than by trusting this comment: the gate scripts call
# scripts/check_gate_scripts_tracked.sh on startup, and that script's default
# list is exactly these four -- so it fails if any one of them is untracked and
# the next wholesale rewrite breaks the build instead of quietly disarming it.
# Keep the two lists in sync: a new gate script needs a negation here AND an
# entry in check_gate_scripts_tracked.sh's GATES array.
# ===========================================================================

# ── Build directories ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /build/ was 1351 tracked files of stale CMake output until task 5 removed it
# from the index; a prebuilt liblgx_runtime.so in the tree can mask a build
# break that would otherwise fail on a clean checkout.
/build/
/build-*/
/build-*-*/
/cmake-build-*/

# ── Compiled objects and libraries ──────────────────────────────────────────
# *.so.* matters: CMake emits liblgx_runtime.so.1 and .so.1.0.1 alongside
# liblgx_runtime.so, and a bare *.so rule leaves the versioned names unignored.
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# ── CMake ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt

# ── Package artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.deb
*.rpm
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.buildinfo
*.changes
*.ddeb

# Packaging output directory. Four artifacts from a 1.0.1 build are still
# tracked here from before this rule existed; git ignores do not untrack, so
# removing them is a separate `git rm --cached` if that is wanted.
/packaging/output/

# ── Security audits (CRITICAL - keep private!) ──────────────────────────────
# These are deliberate, per the project's open-source strategy: a vulnerability
# report committed to a public repository is published whether or not anyone
# reads the commit log. Do not weaken them to tidy the file up.
security_audit_*/
security_audit_report/
security_*.pdf
audit_*.md
vulnerability_*.txt

# ── Test artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
test_results.txt
core
core.*
vgcore.*

# Root-level test/bench binaries (built outputs that should not be committed)
/test_lgx
/test_adaptive
/test_frame_debug
/test_frame_debug_full
/test_frame_stress
/test_basic
/test_alignment
/test_statistics
/test_overflow
/tests/test_adaptive
/tests/test_frame_debug
/tests/test_frame_debug_full
/tests/test_frame_stress
/tests/test_basic
/tests/test_alignment
/tests/test_statistics
/tests/test_overflow

# ── Profiling and coverage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.prof
perf.data
perf.data.old
callgrind.out.*
massif.out.*
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov

# ── Sanitizer output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.san

# ── Personal notes and customer data ────────────────────────────────────────
TODO.txt
NOTES.md
personal/
lead-engineer-new-verdict/
customers/
